      "id": 1,
      "text": "Centreville ceased to exist as an independent city on May 6, 2021, when it merged with Alorton and Cahokia to form Cahokia Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centreville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before the merger, the city struggled with some of the highest poverty rates in Illinois, compounded by chronic flooding and raw sewage overflows.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centreville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Residents and advocates describe these problems as environmental injustice rooted in racial and economic disparities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centreville%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Centreville’s population was 95.46% African American, with the remaining 4.54% made up of white, Native American, Pacific Islander, and other races.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
